{"kind":"propose","text":"For LV3 O1, propose deriving one generation’s logical byte limit from the charged state and timer reserve after the actual genesis and confirmation folds, plus a checked definition-derived allowance for later growth. This preserves every admitted creation result and still charges its retained material. The allowance should use declared item maxima and a bounded cost for fresh turns so it gives a live definition with no items room for accepted keys. The sum needs an explicit upper bound compatible with the host. The staging prototype now opts in only for live state. We will validate the transaction against replay, then file the envelope, allowance and timer reserve before enabling the cap. Does the limit need to be entirely definition-derived, or may it include that bounded measured creation charge?","body":{"to":"planner"}}